---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { DATA, DEVICES, SITE, readingCount } from '../lib/data.ts'

const files = [
  ['/data/v1/devices.json', 'the whole dataset: every device and every reading'],
  ['/data/v1/devices/<id>.json', 'one device, for example /data/v1/devices/iphone-17.json'],
  ['/data/v1/devices.csv', 'one row per device, screen, orientation and runtime; nested fields joined with _'],
  ['/data/v1/schema.json', 'the JSON Schema (draft 2020-12) every file follows'],
  ['/data/v1/version.json', 'the dataset version, its date, and the counts of devices, runtimes and readings'],
  ['/llms.txt', 'an index of the site for language models'],
  ['/llms-full.txt', "every device's current reading as Markdown tables, and the guide"],
]
---
<Base title="screens.guide for coding agents" description="The dataset as JSON, CSV and Markdown, its schema and license, and how to cite it.">
  <h1>For coding agents</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The site's numbers are a dataset first: {DEVICES.length} devices and {readingCount()} readings,
    version {DATA.version} of {DATA.updated}. Fetch the files below, or a Markdown copy of any page.
  </p>

  <h2>Files</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">URL</th><th scope="col">What</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {files.map(([url, what]) => (
          <tr><td><code>{url.includes('<') ? url : <a href={url}>{url}</a>}</code></td><td>{what}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Every page has a Markdown copy at its path plus <code>.md</code>: <a href="/devices/iphone-17.md">/devices/iphone-17.md</a> for <a href="/devices/iphone-17">/devices/iphone-17</a>, and <a href="/index.md">/index.md</a> for the home page. The files allow requests from any origin.
  </p>

  <h2>Reading the data</h2>
  <ul class="prose">
    <li>One reading per device, runtime build, screen and rotation. A device's <code>current</code> names the build to show first: the newest release build with a reading in each screen and rotation.</li>
    <li>Lengths are in the device's <code>unit</code>: points on iOS, dp on Android. Positions are window coordinates from the top left, already rotated for the reading's orientation.</li>
    <li>A value no run measured is <code>null</code>, and the reading's <code>missing</code> gives the reason for that field. Never fill it from another device.</li>
    <li>A reading on a beta build has <code>runtime.prerelease</code> true; its values can change by the release.</li>
    <li><code>cornerRadii</code> has two sets, <code>profile</code> and <code>measured</code>, each with its <code>source</code>. On the iPads on iOS 27.2 and 27.3 they differ.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>License and citation</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    The dataset is licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a>: copy, change and redistribute it, commercially too, with credit. Credit it as "screens.guide, measured by Modaal" with a link to <a href={SITE}>{SITE}</a>, and name the version you used, {DATA.version}. The code and pages are MIT-licensed.
  </p>
</Base>
